(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: TAX EXEMPTION UNDER SECTION 80-IAC OF INCOME TAX ACT \(SECTION 80-IAC\) / INTER-MINISTERIAL BOARD \(IMB\) / CENTRAL BOARD OF DIRECT TAXES \(CBDT\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Eligible startups can get 100% deduction on corporate profits for 3) Tj
T*
(consecutive financial years out of their first 10 years of incorporation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Incorporated as a Private Limited Company or Limited Liability) Tj
T*
(   Partnership \(LLP\).) Tj
T*
(2. Incorporated between 1st April 2016 and 31st March 2025 \(as extended\).) Tj
T*
(3. Annual turnover must not exceed Rs. 100 Crore in any financial year.) Tj
T*
(4. Working towards innovation, development, or commercialization of new) Tj
T*
(   products, processes, or services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. 100% income tax exemption on profits for 3 consecutive assessment years) Tj
T*
(   chosen by the startup within the 10-year period.) Tj
T*
(2. Concession or margin money subsidy rate of 100.0 % subsidy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. DPIIT Certificate of Recognition) Tj
T*
(2. Audited Financial Statements & ITRs since incorporation) Tj
T*
(3. Detailed Video Link explaining product innovation and uniqueness) Tj
T*
(4. Memorandum and Articles of Association \(MoA & AoA\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via Startup India Portal \(Form-1 to IMB\)) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://www.startupindia.gov.in/content/sih/en/tax-exemptions.html) Tj
T*
ET
